WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.910
Well today's council meeting was
actually quite a light agenda, it's my

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.260
first one back around the table and I've
enjoyed being back.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.580
The Ohoka Gatekeepers Lodge has been moved into
the Ohoka Domain

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.100
and that was approved today.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:27.170
and we also are looking at sending some
Councillors over to cement our sister

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.770
city relationship with Enshi which
is a very important part of

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.220
our. international relations.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.700
Today the
council acknowledged Neil Falconer, he

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.400
received the Queen's Service Medal in the
New Year Honours for services to

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.300
communications and broadcasting.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.380
and we also farewelled a very loved colleague Murray Binnie

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.900
who's been our Drainage Manager for many years

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.740
and also bought an understanding of Tikanga Māori and Te Reo into the council.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.980
He's been a big part of our Waiata
group and in fostering our relationship

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.420
with Ngāi Tūāhuriri and he will be very
sorely missed.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.600
From now on our meetings are going to
get a lot busier with LTP coming

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.790
up, our ten year plan, and there's
obviously a lot of discussions to be had

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.400
and a lot of submissions to come in from
the community.

